[{"type_of":"comment","id_code":"3jhhi","created_at":"2026-10-31T10:08:43Z","ai_disclosure_level":"not_disclosed","ai_disclosure_label":"Not Disclosed","body_html":"\u003cp\u003eobserved vs signed listing is a really honest split. curious if buyers will actually treat them differently or just go with whatever shows the price they want\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","user":{"name":"Hiten Sethiya","username":"hitensethiya","twitter_username":null,"github_username":"HitenSethiya","user_id":3922767,"website_url":null,"profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3922767%2F3fe89ed1-b28d-46c7-a690-4e4fa773b975.jpeg","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3922767%2F3fe89ed1-b28d-46c7-a690-4e4fa773b975.jpeg"},"children":[{"type_of":"comment","id_code":"3jhi4","created_at":"2026-10-31T10:18:26Z","ai_disclosure_level":"not_disclosed","ai_disclosure_label":"Not Disclosed","body_html":"\u003cp\u003eWe don’t know yet whether buyers will treat them differently. The API already keeps observed offers separate from signed catalogs, and we can make that distinction clearer in the buying interface: what was observed, who signed what, and when it was checked. A signature still doesn’t prove delivery. The next question is whether showing that evidence changes a buyer’s choice—we haven’t measured that yet.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","user":{"name":"Alex","username":"alexar76","twitter_username":"build_ai_infra","github_username":null,"user_id":3927872,"website_url":"https://github.com/alexar76","profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg"},"children":[]}]},{"type_of":"comment","id_code":"3jhl8","created_at":"2026-10-31T11:40:43Z","ai_disclosure_level":"not_disclosed","ai_disclosure_label":"Not Disclosed","body_html":"\u003cp\u003eThat TensorFeed trial detail changes the math. How do you probe a route for a price without spending the seller's free calls?\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","user":{"name":"Odinaka Robert Nnamani","username":"robertpaschal","twitter_username":null,"github_username":"Robertpaschal","user_id":2167197,"website_url":"https://heypascal.me","profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F2167197%2Fecea0dc6-e64a-4d17-86da-0ec53a674663.jpeg","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F2167197%2Fecea0dc6-e64a-4d17-86da-0ec53a674663.jpeg"},"children":[{"type_of":"comment","id_code":"3ji5i","created_at":"2026-10-31T14:18:54Z","ai_disclosure_level":"not_disclosed","ai_disclosure_label":"Not Disclosed","body_html":"\u003cp\u003eWe don't have a general way yet, and that's why TensorFeed isn't listed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eToday the probe is one unpaid request per route. If a route answers for free, we don't list it and skip that seller's other routes until the next cycle. At the default six-hour interval that caps it at four free calls a day, but those are still calls the seller serves for nothing, so we haven't turned it on for TensorFeed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eTheir discovery document already names a price and a payTo for each route. What the probe adds is evidence that the live route asks for that price and pays that address. Without it, we could list the document's figures, labelled as the seller's published price rather than an observation, or not list the route. For now we don't list it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe clean fix has to come from the seller: a header or a HEAD request that returns the 402 without serving the call or counting it against the trial. That's the question TensorFeed would need to answer.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","user":{"name":"Alex","username":"alexar76","twitter_username":"build_ai_infra","github_username":null,"user_id":3927872,"website_url":"https://github.com/alexar76","profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg"},"children":[{"type_of":"comment","id_code":"3jia3","created_at":"2026-10-31T15:40:54Z","ai_disclosure_level":"not_disclosed","ai_disclosure_label":"Not Disclosed","body_html":"\u003cp\u003eA HEAD check that returns 402 without burning a free call would settle it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","user":{"name":"Odinaka Robert Nnamani","username":"robertpaschal","twitter_username":null,"github_username":"Robertpaschal","user_id":2167197,"website_url":"https://heypascal.me","profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F2167197%2Fecea0dc6-e64a-4d17-86da-0ec53a674663.jpeg","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F2167197%2Fecea0dc6-e64a-4d17-86da-0ec53a674663.jpeg"},"children":[{"type_of":"comment","id_code":"3jikh","created_at":"2026-10-31T18:46:40Z","ai_disclosure_level":"not_disclosed","ai_disclosure_label":"Not Disclosed","body_html":"\u003cp\u003eOnly if the seller answers HEAD before the free tier, and by default most don't. Express, and Starlette on GET routes, answer HEAD by running the GET handler, so the free call is spent anyway; on a POST-only route HEAD gets a 404 or 405 with no price in it. So it's one rule on the seller's side: answer HEAD with the 402 before checking the trial. If a seller does that, trying HEAD first is a small change for us, falling back to the unpaid request only when HEAD returns no 402.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","user":{"name":"Alex","username":"alexar76","twitter_username":"build_ai_infra","github_username":null,"user_id":3927872,"website_url":"https://github.com/alexar76","profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg"},"children":[{"type_of":"comment","id_code":"3jin1","created_at":"2026-10-31T19:45:14Z","ai_disclosure_level":"not_disclosed","ai_disclosure_label":"Not Disclosed","body_html":"\u003cp\u003eThat default behaviour kills the idea for most sellers. A HEAD answer before the free tier check is the only version that keeps the probe cheap.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","user":{"name":"Odinaka Robert Nnamani","username":"robertpaschal","twitter_username":null,"github_username":"Robertpaschal","user_id":2167197,"website_url":"https://heypascal.me","profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F2167197%2Fecea0dc6-e64a-4d17-86da-0ec53a674663.jpeg","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F2167197%2Fecea0dc6-e64a-4d17-86da-0ec53a674663.jpeg"},"children":[{"type_of":"comment","id_code":"3jjia","created_at":"2026-11-01T06:08:48Z","ai_disclosure_level":"not_disclosed","ai_disclosure_label":"Not Disclosed","body_html":"\u003cp\u003eWe shipped it this morning. The hub now sends HEAD first: a 402 with the terms in the x402 V2 PAYMENT-REQUIRED header is the whole check, with no second request. A 2xx to HEAD means the call was already served free, so we stop there. Only when HEAD brings no price (a 404 or 405, or a 402 with the terms only in the body) do we fall back to the single unpaid request. Our own gateway answers HEAD that way, so checking it costs nothing.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","user":{"name":"Alex","username":"alexar76","twitter_username":"build_ai_infra","github_username":null,"user_id":3927872,"website_url":"https://github.com/alexar76","profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg"},"children":[{"type_of":"comment","id_code":"3jjp4","created_at":"2026-11-01T08:39:38Z","ai_disclosure_level":"not_disclosed","ai_disclosure_label":"Not Disclosed","body_html":"\u003cp\u003eShipping the HEAD check the same morning is a quick turnaround, and stopping at a 2xx keeps the probe cheap.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","user":{"name":"Odinaka Robert Nnamani","username":"robertpaschal","twitter_username":null,"github_username":"Robertpaschal","user_id":2167197,"website_url":"https://heypascal.me","profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F2167197%2Fecea0dc6-e64a-4d17-86da-0ec53a674663.jpeg","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F2167197%2Fecea0dc6-e64a-4d17-86da-0ec53a674663.jpeg"},"children":[]}]}]}]}]}]}]},{"type_of":"comment","id_code":"3jj7b","created_at":"2026-11-01T02:07:59Z","ai_disclosure_level":"not_disclosed","ai_disclosure_label":"Not Disclosed","body_html":"\u003cp\u003eThat feedback is a better product signal than marketplace sign-ups. Sellers need a measurable path from integration work to qualified demand, not another profile to maintain. I’d test a thin integration that proves time-to-first-value and tracks the distribution channel that created the lead before expanding the catalog.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","user":{"name":"Alex Shev","username":"alexshev","twitter_username":"AlexshevPm","github_username":null,"user_id":3812101,"website_url":"https://terminalskills.io/","profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3812101%2F0946c1f5-f8a5-464c-bf18-10850a434ef9.png","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3812101%2F0946c1f5-f8a5-464c-bf18-10850a434ef9.png"},"children":[{"type_of":"comment","id_code":"3jjhd","created_at":"2026-11-01T06:00:09Z","ai_disclosure_level":"not_disclosed","ai_disclosure_label":"Not Disclosed","body_html":"\u003cp\u003eAgreed. The thinnest version we could build is now live: the seller does no integration at all. With its consent, the hub reads the discovery document the seller already publishes and checks the price with a single HEAD request. The half you describe as qualified demand is still open: no outside seller is listed this way yet, so there is no demand number to show.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","user":{"name":"Alex","username":"alexar76","twitter_username":"build_ai_infra","github_username":null,"user_id":3927872,"website_url":"https://github.com/alexar76","profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg"},"children":[]}]},{"type_of":"comment","id_code":"3jmh9","created_at":"2026-11-02T08:51:39Z","ai_disclosure_level":"not_disclosed","ai_disclosure_label":"Not Disclosed","body_html":"\u003cp\u003eThe twelve-hour expiry raises a small caching question: can repeated reads ever keep an observed offer alive? I'd want observation time to stay fixed until a successful probe replaces it, even if the listing is popular. This \u003ca href=\"https://prachub.com/interview-questions/design-a-ttl-aware-lru-cache-without-full-expiration-scans?utm_source=devto\u0026amp;utm_campaign=v1012\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\"\u003eTTL cache question\u003c/a\u003e separates recency from expiration in a nice compact way. I'd also test a failed refresh right before expiry so the last good quote doesn't quietly become a fresh one.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","user":{"name":"Emily Woods","username":"emilywoodsnyc","twitter_username":null,"github_username":null,"user_id":3912599,"website_url":null,"profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3912599%2Fc95a7ee1-41d2-4e1e-994d-e1aedab86d39.png","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3912599%2Fc95a7ee1-41d2-4e1e-994d-e1aedab86d39.png"},"children":[{"type_of":"comment","id_code":"3jmik","created_at":"2026-11-02T09:11:54Z","ai_disclosure_level":"not_disclosed","ai_disclosure_label":"Not Disclosed","body_html":"\u003cp\u003eNo. The observed time is written only by the hub's own observation cycle (every six hours per seller), never by a read, so a popular listing cannot keep an offer alive: it drops out twelve hours after its last successful probe however often it is read. Each listed route carries the time of its own successful probe.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eA failed refresh never freshens the old quote. If the refresh reaches the seller but gets no usable 402 (no discovery document, a timeout on the route, a different payTo, or a call served for free), that observation replaces the old one and the route is withdrawn at once. If the observation fails before it can say anything, nothing is written: the last good quote keeps its original time and expires twelve hours after it. We added a test for exactly the case you describe, a refresh failing a minute before expiry.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n","user":{"name":"Alex","username":"alexar76","twitter_username":"build_ai_infra","github_username":null,"user_id":3927872,"website_url":"https://github.com/alexar76","profile_image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=640,height=640,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg","profile_image_90":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=90,height=90,fit=cover,gravity=auto,format=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Fuser%2Fprofile_image%2F3927872%2Fdf501cac-6862-47af-8b22-4e3067696337.jpeg"},"children":[]}]}]